Hi All!

Currently, adMisc is a double array that serves a couple of roles:

1. passing things that are actually part of the response to coxph (event indicator)
2. passing parameters such as the number of degrees of freedom to the t distribution

I would like to change that by:

1. changing adY to be a matrix (from Terry's idea), with distribution-defined number of columns.
2. changing adMisc to be distribution-defined, which I can unpack using standard Rcpp-isms.

This will also help to simplify the definition of the distributions to something kind of like

double Deviance(const CDataset& data, const bag& my_bag);

(etc)

Any thoughts?

PS. Shouldn't the t distribution also have a scale parameter - i.e. we just do a standard t?

pdm

